UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Newton''s Laws of Motion

## Key Concepts
- **First Law (Inertia):** A body remains at rest or in uniform motion unless acted upon by a net external force.
- **Second Law:** F = ma — Force equals mass times acceleration.
- **Third Law:** For every action there is an equal and opposite reaction.

## Important Formulas
- F = ma
- p = mv (momentum)
- F = dp/dt
- Friction: f = μN

## CET Tips
- Always draw a free-body diagram.
- Resolve forces along and perpendicular to motion.
- Watch units (SI throughout).' WHERE id='71a436e2-4d33-464a-8ca3-e7894ed57218';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Kinematics

## Equations of Motion (constant a)
- v = u + at
- s = ut + ½at²
- v² = u² + 2as

## Projectile Motion
- Range R = u² sin(2θ)/g
- Max height H = u² sin²θ/(2g)
- Time of flight T = 2u sinθ / g

## Tips
- For relative motion, use vector subtraction.
- Plot v–t graphs to visualise displacement (area under curve).' WHERE id='4e8d7e59-bd4c-4887-a839-69b2bc8d7645';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Thermodynamics

## Laws
- **Zeroth Law:** Thermal equilibrium is transitive.
- **First Law:** ΔU = Q − W
- **Second Law:** Entropy of an isolated system never decreases.

## Processes
- Isothermal: PV = const
- Adiabatic: PVᵞ = const
- Efficiency of Carnot engine: η = 1 − T_c/T_h' WHERE id='22de5236-def5-4b52-94ca-3d9dc877db2e';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Electrostatics

## Coulomb''s Law
F = kq₁q₂/r²,  k = 9×10⁹ N·m²/C²

## Electric Field & Potential
- E = F/q
- V = kQ/r
- Capacitance: C = Q/V; for parallel plate C = ε₀A/d' WHERE id='42ddfff5-ad1f-408d-b3d8-5e9bf76439cd';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Atomic Structure

## Models
- Thomson, Rutherford, Bohr, Quantum mechanical.

## Bohr Model (H atom)
- E_n = −13.6/n² eV
- r_n = 0.529 n² Å

## Quantum Numbers
n, l, m_l, m_s — define orbitals and electron states.' WHERE id='ab96f794-5dbb-40b7-88d6-f6fe63c1e396';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Chemical Bonding

## Types
- Ionic, covalent, coordinate, metallic, hydrogen bonding.

## VSEPR
Predicts molecular geometry by minimising lone-pair repulsion.

## Hybridisation
sp, sp², sp³, sp³d, sp³d² — link to geometry & bond angles.' WHERE id='f217bceb-3838-4e4a-be93-b5e149994d65';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Organic Chemistry Basics

## Hydrocarbons
- Alkanes (CnH2n+2), alkenes (CnH2n), alkynes (CnH2n−2).

## IUPAC Nomenclature
Identify longest chain → number from end giving lowest locants → name substituents alphabetically.

## Reaction Types
Substitution, addition, elimination, oxidation, reduction.' WHERE id='43ca2e08-f486-48c4-9d14-bde170e47f85';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Thermodynamics

## Laws
- **Zeroth Law:** Thermal equilibrium is transitive.
- **First Law:** ΔU = Q − W
- **Second Law:** Entropy of an isolated system never decreases.

## Processes
- Isothermal: PV = const
- Adiabatic: PVᵞ = const
- Efficiency of Carnot engine: η = 1 − T_c/T_h' WHERE id='5611987e-289a-421c-9cb6-db7a808a969f';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Integration

## Standard Integrals
- ∫xⁿ dx = xⁿ⁺¹/(n+1) + C
- ∫1/x dx = ln|x| + C
- ∫eˣ dx = eˣ + C
- ∫sin x dx = −cos x + C

## Techniques
Substitution, by parts (∫u dv = uv − ∫v du), partial fractions.

## Definite Integrals
∫ₐᵇ f(x)dx = F(b) − F(a)' WHERE id='36324892-9f50-4260-90f8-b8e40bd2f224';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Differentiation

## Standard Derivatives
- d(xⁿ)/dx = nxⁿ⁻¹
- d(sin x)/dx = cos x
- d(eˣ)/dx = eˣ

## Rules
Product, quotient, chain rule.

## Applications
Maxima/minima (f''(x)=0, check f''''), tangents, rate problems.' WHERE id='2731390a-fb5d-488c-845a-7c6834d9252c';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Trigonometry

## Identities
- sin²θ + cos²θ = 1
- 1 + tan²θ = sec²θ
- sin(A±B), cos(A±B), tan(A±B) formulas

## Inverse Functions
Range, principal values, identities.' WHERE id='617cffa9-3e0a-4169-adbb-802b0c03dc69';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Vectors

## Operations
Addition (triangle/parallelogram), dot product (a·b = |a||b|cosθ), cross product (a×b = |a||b|sinθ n̂).

## Applications
Work W = F·d, torque τ = r×F, area of parallelogram |a×b|.' WHERE id='95c692e5-a4c5-4806-a0a7-96585ce3b036';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Cell Biology

## Cell Theory
All living things are made of cells; cells arise from pre-existing cells.

## Organelles
Nucleus (DNA), mitochondria (ATP), ER, Golgi, ribosomes, lysosomes, chloroplast (plants).

## Cell Division
Mitosis (somatic), Meiosis (gametes).' WHERE id='8db8ba00-be32-423c-83b2-222afcc0cea0';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Genetics

## Mendel''s Laws
Segregation, independent assortment, dominance.

## Molecular Basis
DNA → RNA → Protein (Central dogma). Codons, mutations.

## Inheritance Patterns
Autosomal dominant/recessive, X-linked.' WHERE id='bc40e2dc-a318-4d0f-9bca-ca8b9c60f640';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Human Physiology

## Major Systems
Digestive, respiratory, circulatory, nervous, endocrine, excretory.

## Key Numbers
Normal pulse 60–100 bpm, BP 120/80 mmHg, blood pH 7.35–7.45.' WHERE id='39299af9-cd96-4798-88eb-1b3b94f68117';
UPDATE topics SET notes_md='# Photosynthesis

## Overall Reaction
6CO₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂  (light energy)

## Stages
- Light reactions (thylakoids): produce ATP, NADPH, O₂.
- Calvin cycle (stroma): fixes CO₂ via RuBisCO.' WHERE id='12cb67c7-0cdd-4bd2-8bba-1c07dca53e1a';
